.TH FLEET-HEALTH 1 "2026-11-25" "cti-agent" "CTI Agent Fleet"
.SH NAME
fleet-health \- the lanes' health reports, for the check-in and for a person
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fleet\-health delta \-\-pending
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-home
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-list
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-state
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B fleet\-health commit \-\-pending
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-home
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-state
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B fleet\-health show
.RB [ \-\-home
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-list
.IR FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every lane is held to one contract: it writes
.I $FLEET_HOME/reports/health/<lane>.json
(schema
.BR cti\-lane\-health/1 )
with what it should have covered, what it did, and each gap. A gap the
organization declared on purpose, in its org pack's
.I expected\-gaps.txt
with a reason, is marked by design; every other gap is an accident.
.PP
.B delta
compares each report with what earlier check-in beats were told (the state
file) and prints only the difference, as the
.B LANE HEALTH
block
.BR run\-checkin (1)
puts at the top of the beat's prompt: a new accident, one that cleared, a
report that went missing, stale or came back, and a declaration that is
about to expire or matches nothing. With nothing changed it prints one line.
The state the beat will have been told is written to
.BR \-\-pending .
.PP
.B commit
saves that state, once the beat has finished, so each change reaches the
model once. A beat that failed is not committed, and the next beat is told
the same changes.
.PP
.B show
prints every lane's report, one line each: coverage, open accidents, gaps by
design, and age.
.PP
It reads only the fleet's own files: the reports, the lanes' health
contracts
.RI ( $FLEET_CODE/share/health.list ,
generated from the lane manifests),
.B FLEET_LANES
(lanes this box does not run are skipped) and the state file. It sends
nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-home " DIR"
The fleet's home, with reports/health and state/ under it. Default:
.B $FLEET_HOME
or /var/lib/cti\-agent.
.TP
.BI \-\-list " FILE"
The lanes' health contracts. Default:
.IR $FLEET_CODE/share/health.list .
.TP
.BI \-\-pending " FILE"
.BR delta :
write the next state here.
.BR commit :
the state to save.
.TP
.BI \-\-state " FILE"
The state file. Default:
.IR $FLEET_HOME/state/health\-seen.json .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when the lane list or a file it must write cannot be used;
2 for a bad command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo cti\-agent fleet\-health show
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-checkin (1),
.BR run\-appaudit (1),
.BR cti\-agent\-doctor (1)
